---
import ServicePage from '../layouts/ServicePage.astro';
import { general } from '../data/qa';
import photo from '../assets/photos/ropes.jpg';
---

<ServicePage
  title="About Shore Leave | Zak and Bozzy, Auckland"
  description="Shore Leave exists because nobody has anything left at the end of a weekend on the water. Meet Zak and Bozzy, and why we started this."
  crumb="About"
  h1="Nobody wants to scrub a deck on Sunday night."
  lede="We're Zak and Bozzy. Shore Leave is a small Auckland business built around one simple problem."
  photo={photo}
  photoAlt="Heavy rope coiled around a pair of bollards on a boat's deck"
  faqs={[general[4]]}
  links={[
    { href: '/book', label: 'Book a reset' },
    { href: '/how-it-works', label: 'How it works' },
  ]}
>
  <section class="wrap band lg:grid lg:grid-cols-12 lg:gap-12">
    <h2 class="lg:col-span-5">Why this exists</h2>
    <div class="lg:col-span-6 lg:col-start-7 mt-4 lg:mt-2 grid gap-4 text-lg">
      <p>A good day on the water finishes you off. You've had the sun, the salt and the kids. You've still got to get the boat in, the gear off and everyone home.</p>
      <p>By then, nobody has anything left. The deck stays salty, the rubbish stays aboard and the fridge goes warm. The boat sits like that until the next trip, which starts with an hour of cleaning up after the last one.</p>
      <p>We think that's backwards. Hotels don't ask you to change the sheets before you check out. So we built the service we'd want: you get off the boat, and we reset it.</p>
    </div>
  </section>
</ServicePage>
